  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1... \nNew day, same message. High pressure remains in control, with\ndry weather highly likely through Saturday. The passage of a\n500mb ridge axis will provide a small boost to already above-\nnormal temperatures on Monday.\n\nA dry frontal passage Monday night will provide some clouds and\na minor temperature bump downward, but not enough moisture for \nprecipitation chances. That boundary then returns north as a\nwarm front through midweek, which will eventually push\ntemperatures some 10 to 15 degrees above normal by Thursday. A\nshortwave crossing the Great Lakes Thursday night/Friday appears\nto still remain too far north for precipitation chances; a cloud\nincrease is expected north of Pittsburgh.\n\nThere is still a decent model signal for an Ohio Valley\nshortwave next weekend that may finally break the dry spell on\nSunday. The various ensemble members still show strength and\ntiming differences, so rainfall could get pushed later once\nagain, but a wetter post-Halloween pattern is certainly\npossible.",
